.nh
.TH "PB-ENV-UNSET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-unset - Remove one environment variable


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env unset <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove one environment variable

.PP
Delete one ENV name from the selected personal, team, or host scope. The confirmation code confirms removal. Previously selected recipients receive a refreshed encrypted delivery with the deleted value omitted; running processes retain their environment.

.PP
ENV values are encrypted before they leave the client. Commands select personal, team, or host scope explicitly; list output shows metadata rather than secret values. Unlock the local vault when a key operation requires it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	six-character confirmation code from the preview

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for unset

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print redacted JSON metadata

.PP
\fB--machine\fP=""
	Personal override for an owned machine, even in a Team workspace; omitted uses the active workspace

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team scope; cannot be combined with --machine


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP
